  "title": "First modern Olympic Games, Athens",
  "summary": "From 6 to 15 April 1896 Athens staged the first international Olympic Games of the modern era, run by the International Olympic Committee created at a Paris congress in 1894. Fourteen nations and 241 male athletes, figures sources dispute, contested nine sports, with the marble-refurbished Panathenaic Stadium as the main venue. Spyridon Louis of Greece won the marathon, the highlight of the Games for the host nation.",
